#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:4
msgid "フェルミ準位と占有数"
msgstr "Fermi Level and Occupation Numbers"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:6
msgid ""
":ref:`エネルギーバンド<bandstructure>`\\ に、電子がどのように入るかを考える。 "
"電子数と温度から占有数を決め、金属のフェルミ面と半導体のキャリア密度の計算につなげる。"
msgstr ""
"We consider how electrons fill :ref:`energy bands <bandstructure>`\\ . "
"From the electron count and temperature, we determine the occupation "
"numbers. This connects the occupation numbers to the Fermi surface in "
"metals and to the calculation of carrier densities in semiconductors."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:9
msgid "**前提知識**: :ref:`バンド構造と状態密度<bandstructure>`、:ref:`半充填<half-filling>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Band Structure and Density of States "
"<bandstructure>` and :ref:`Half Filling <half-filling>`."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:11
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:13
msgid "フェルミ–ディラック分布で占有数を表し、電子数から化学ポテンシャルが決まることを説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Express occupation numbers using the Fermi–Dirac distribution and explain"
" how the electron count determines the chemical potential."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:14
msgid "絶対零度でのフェルミ面と、金属と半導体でのフェルミ準位の意味を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain the Fermi surface at absolute zero and the meaning of the Fermi "
"level in metals and semiconductors."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:15
msgid "ボルツマン近似が使える条件と、そのときの占有数の形を導く。"
msgstr ""
"Derive the conditions for the Boltzmann approximation and the resulting "
"expressions for the occupation numbers."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:20
msgid "フェルミ–ディラック分布"
msgstr "Fermi–Dirac Distribution"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:22
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"エネルギー :math:`E` の1電子状態を考える。熱平衡での平均占有数 :math:`f(E)` は、 電子の化学ポテンシャルを "
":math:`\\mu`、温度を :math:`T`、ボルツマン定数を :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}` "
"とすると、次のフェルミ–ディラック分布に従う。"
msgstr ""
"Consider a one-electron state of energy :math:`E`. At thermal "
"equilibrium, its mean occupation number :math:`f(E)` follows the "
"Fermi–Dirac distribution. With electron chemical potential :math:`\\mu`, "
"temperature :math:`T`, and Boltzmann constant :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}`, the"
" distribution is"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:26
#, python-brace-format
msgid "f(E)=\\frac{1}{1+\\exp[(E-\\mu)/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]}"
msgstr "f(E)=\\frac{1}{1+\\exp[(E-\\mu)/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]}"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:31
msgid ""
"ここでの1電子状態はスピンを含めて区別し、各状態には電子が最大1個入る。 所定の電子数になるよう :math:`\\sum_\\alpha "
"f(E_\\alpha)` を合わせることで :math:`\\mu` が決まる。:math:`\\alpha` "
"は波数、バンド、スピンで指定した状態を表す。 :ref:`状態密度<density-of-states>`\\ "
"が分かれば、状態の和をエネルギー積分に置き換えられる。 有限温度で :math:`E=\\mu` の状態があれば、その平均占有数は "
":math:`1/2` である。"
msgstr ""
"Each one-electron state here includes a spin designation and can hold at "
"most one electron. Setting :math:`\\sum_\\alpha f(E_\\alpha)` equal to "
"the specified electron count determines :math:`\\mu`. The index "
":math:`\\alpha` denotes a state specified by its wave vector, band, and "
"spin. If the :ref:`density of states <density-of-states>`\\  is known, an"
" energy integral can replace the sum over states. At finite temperature, "
"any state with :math:`E=\\mu` has a mean occupation number of "
":math:`1/2`."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:37
msgid ""
":numref:`fig-fermi-occupation-temperature`\\ では、温度が高いほど占有数が変わる "
"エネルギー範囲が広い。有限温度の曲線はすべて :math:`(E,f)=(\\mu,1/2)` を通る。"
msgstr ""
"In :numref:`fig-fermi-occupation-temperature`\\ , the energy range over "
"which the occupation number changes grows wider as the temperature rises."
" All finite-temperature curves pass through :math:`(E,f)=(\\mu,1/2)`."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:40
msgid "化学ポテンシャルを中心に1から0へ変化する占有数。絶対零度では段差があり、有限温度では温度が高いほど変化がなだらかになる。"
msgstr ""
"The occupation number changes from one to zero around the chemical "
"potential. There is a step at absolute zero. At finite temperatures, the "
"change becomes more gradual as the temperature rises."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:46
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"式 :eq:`f(E)` を、横軸のエネルギーを :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T_1` で割って描いた。 実線は温度 "
":math:`T_1`、一点鎖線は :math:`2.5T_1`、灰色の破線は絶対零度に近づけた極限。 黒丸は有限温度での "
":math:`f(\\mu)=1/2` を示す。"
msgstr ""
"Plot of Equation :eq:`f(E)` with the energy on the horizontal axis "
"divided by :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T_1`. The solid curve is for temperature "
":math:`T_1`, the dash-dotted curve is for :math:`2.5T_1`, and the gray "
"dashed curve is the limit as the temperature approaches absolute zero. "
"The black dot marks :math:`f(\\mu)=1/2` at finite temperature."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:53
msgid "絶対零度とフェルミ面"
msgstr "Absolute Zero and the Fermi Surface"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:55
msgid ""
":math:`T\\to0` では、:math:`E<\\mu` の占有数は1に、:math:`E>\\mu` の占有数は0に "
"近づく。絶対零度での化学ポテンシャルをフェルミエネルギーと呼ぶ。半導体では有限温度の :math:`\\mu` "
"もフェルミ準位と呼ぶことが多い。絶対零度で化学ポテンシャルが :ref:`バンドギャップ<valence-conduction-band-"
"gap>`\\ 内にあるとき、ギャップ内でその値を動かしても各状態の占有は変わらない。"
msgstr ""
"As :math:`T\\to0`, the occupation number approaches one for "
":math:`E<\\mu` and zero for :math:`E>\\mu`. The chemical potential at "
"absolute zero is called the Fermi energy. In semiconductors, :math:`\\mu`"
" at finite temperature is also often called the Fermi level. If the "
"chemical potential lies within the :ref:`band gap <valence-conduction-"
"band-gap>`\\  at absolute zero, moving it within the gap leaves the "
"occupation of each state unchanged."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:60
msgid ""
"金属では、少なくとも一つのバンドがフェルミ準位を横切る。波数空間で :math:`E_j(\\boldsymbol k)=\\mu` "
"を満たす面がフェルミ面である。 等間隔な\\ :ref:`1次元のタイト・バインディング鎖<tightbinding>`\\ "
"で最近接ホッピングだけを含めると、1原子1軌道の バンドに、スピンを含めて 原子数の2倍の状態がある。原子1個あたり電子1個の\\ "
":ref:`半充填<half-filling>`\\ では、 フェルミ面に相当する境界は2つのフェルミ点 "
":math:`k=\\pm\\pi/(2a)` になる。 金属では、この\\ :ref:`占有数の段差<kpoint-fermi-"
"surface>`\\ がk点メッシュによる積分誤差に影響する。"
msgstr ""
"In a metal, at least one band crosses the Fermi level. The surface in "
"wave-vector space satisfying :math:`E_j(\\boldsymbol k)=\\mu` is the "
"Fermi surface. With only nearest-neighbor hopping in an equally spaced \\"
" :ref:`one-dimensional tight-binding chain <tightbinding>`\\ , a band "
"with one orbital per atom has twice as many states as atoms, counting "
"spin. At \\ :ref:`half filling <half-filling>`\\ , with one electron per "
"atom, the boundary corresponding to the Fermi surface consists of two "
"Fermi points :math:`k=\\pm\\pi/(2a)`. In metals, this \\ :ref:`step in "
"the occupation number <kpoint-fermi-surface>`\\  affects the integration "
"error of a k-point mesh."

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:71
msgid "ボルツマン近似"
msgstr "Boltzmann Approximation"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:73
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`E-\\mu\\gg k_{\\mathrm B}T` では、式 :eq:`f(E)` の分母で指数項が支配的になる。 "
"したがって伝導帯の電子のように、この条件を満たす状態の占有数は"
msgstr ""
"For :math:`E-\\mu\\gg k_{\\mathrm B}T`, the exponential term dominates "
"the denominator of Equation :eq:`f(E)`. Thus, for states that satisfy "
"this condition, such as electron states in the conduction band, the "
"occupation number is approximated by"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:76
msgid "f(E)\\simeq \\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{E-\\mu}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"
msgstr "f(E)\\simeq \\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{E-\\mu}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"と近似できる。価電子帯の正孔の確率は、その電子状態が空である確率 :math:`1-f(E)` である。:math:`\\mu-E\\gg "
"k_{\\mathrm B}T` では、分母の :math:`\\exp[(E-\\mu)/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]` が小さいため、"
msgstr ""
"The probability of a hole in the valence band is the probability "
":math:`1-f(E)` that the electron state is empty. When :math:`\\mu-E\\gg "
"k_{\\mathrm B}T`, the term :math:`\\exp[(E-\\mu)/(k_{\\mathrm B}T)]` in "
"the denominator is small. The resulting approximation is"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:85
msgid "f(E)\\simeq 1-\\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{\\mu-E}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"
msgstr "f(E)\\simeq 1-\\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{\\mu-E}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:90
msgid "となり、正孔の確率は"
msgstr "and the hole probability is"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:92
msgid "1-f(E)\\simeq \\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{\\mu-E}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"
msgstr "1-f(E)\\simeq \\exp\\!\\left[-\\frac{\\mu-E}{k_{\\mathrm B}T}\\right]"

#: ../../solid/fermi_level_and_occupation.rst:97
msgid ""
"となる。これらの近似から\\ :ref:`伝導帯の電子密度<conduction-band-electrons>`\\ と "
":ref:`価電子帯の正孔密度<valence-band-holes>`\\ を求められる。フェルミ準位がバンド端に近づくと近似の条件が "
"崩れるので、その場合は式 :eq:`f(E)` を状態密度との積分に使う。"
msgstr ""
"These approximations give the \\ :ref:`electron density in the conduction"
" band <conduction-band-electrons>`\\  and the :ref:`hole density in the "
"valence band <valence-band-holes>`\\ . When the Fermi level approaches a "
"band edge, the condition for the approximation breaks down. In that case,"
" use Equation :eq:`f(E)` in the integral with the density of states."

